ASoC: codecs: lpass-va-macro: accept the v2.2 core of SM6375/SM4375

The VA macro of SM6375 and SM4375 (holi, blair) reports core version 2.2.0,
which va_macro_set_lpass_codec_version() does not know, so the probe fails
with "VA Macro v2.2.0 is not supported" and the RX and TX macros, which take
their fsgen clock from it, never probe either. The downstream kernel calls this
LPASS codec bolero 2.1 (qcom,bolero-version = <5>); its register layout is the
pre-2.5 one, which the RX macro handles together for 2.0 and 2.1. Treat 2.2 as
LPASS_CODEC_VERSION_2_1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
index dbc5795b9..44ad69e0f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
@@ -1508,6 +1508,10 @@ static int va_macro_set_lpass_codec_version(struct va_macro *va)
 		case 0:
 			version = LPASS_CODEC_VERSION_2_0;
 			break;
+		case 2:
+			/* SM6375/SM4375 (holi, blair): downstream calls it bolero 2.1 */
+			version = LPASS_CODEC_VERSION_2_1;
+			break;
 		case 5:
 			version = LPASS_CODEC_VERSION_2_5;
 			break;
